WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:02.270
I think Benza is, is amazing at teaching

00:02.370 --> 00:04.270
you how to think about using Claude

00:04.330 --> 00:04.550
Code.

00:04.550 --> 00:05.790
I’ve been to other AI bootcamps where

00:05.810 --> 00:06.910
you’re just, like, copying and pasting

00:06.990 --> 00:07.990
templates, and you’re not really, not

00:08.030 --> 00:09.890
really thinking about how to best leverage

00:10.390 --> 00:10.770
Claude.

00:10.770 --> 00:12.350
He, he writes his own amazing operating

00:12.430 --> 00:14.329
system, and you learn so much so quickly.

00:14.990 --> 00:17.190
I feel like I’m walking out as a builder,

00:17.650 --> 00:20.610
and, uh, I no longer have this fear

00:20.690 --> 00:22.090
like I’m just a beginner, I’m catching

00:22.150 --> 00:22.670
up.
